# Keep generated caches ignored after the project-skill unignore rules above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# --- Large binary CAD, mesh and render artifacts -----------------------------
# These stay on local disk (this repository is still their source of truth) but
# are not pushed. GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB, and the CAD work
# under .trellis/tasks/ holds >10 GB of Fusion archives, mesh exports and
# animation frames. Every evidence package records the SHA-256 of its own
# binaries, so provenance survives without the bytes being in git history.

# Fusion and FreeCAD working archives - regenerable from the cloud document.
*.f3d
*.fcstd
*.fcstd1
*.fcbak

# Bulk mesh, package and video formats.
*.3mf
*.glb
*.zip
*.mp4
*.m4s

# Animation frame sequences.
**/frames/
**/*-frames/

# Mesh exports are large.
*.stl

# Whole-scene STEP exports are regenerable from the Fusion document.
*-scene-*.step

# Scratch directory - working files only, never a deliverable.
/tmp/

# --- Binary artifacts: local only, never pushed ------------------------------
# Only text and code go to the remote. Renders, photographs, CAD, mesh and PDF
# sources stay on local disk, which remains their source of truth; each
# evidence package records their SHA-256 so provenance is preserved.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.pdf
*.step
*.stp
*.igs
*.iges
*.obj
*.dae
*.mtl
*.ply
*.sldprt
*.sldasm
*.dwg
*.gcode
*.backup
